And so with the countdown, sometimes people have said the timer is going up. It's not going down. What the what the blazes is that? Well, it's because the frequencies are just kind of messing with it. It's still run the program, but it can mess with the frequencies.

00:03:08,260 --> 00:03:20,260
If you have a tendency to leave your computer open and run your program, it can throw off the communication from the computer to the generator.

00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:32,260
Not this time. Let's say it's running and it, but next time the computer next time you hit try to run a program, it doesn't read the generator because you threw off that connection.

00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:46,260
So the solution to that is to number one, just keep close your computer when you run a program, so you don't have that because it puts the computer to sleep and the computer is now, you know, not being affected by the frequencies.

00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:54,260
But if that does happen, then, you know, just shut everything down, turn your computer down, reboot it and it should be just fun.

